1. Definitions and scope

"Licensor" means the copyright holder or holders of the Covered Materials.
Permissions outside this License must be obtained from the Licensor or a
representative authorized to grant them. The project maintainer is the initial
contact; a sponsor is not, merely by sponsoring the project, the Licensor.

"Covered Materials" means the original application code, scripts, Skills
(including their instructions and reference text), and documentation supplied
with this License as AI Character Modeling Kit, also previously named ELYTH
Avatar Kit or Chara Kit. It includes copies and modifications of those materials.
It does not include materials identified as separately licensed under Section 8.

"You" means the individual using the Covered Materials for their own purposes,
or the business or organization on whose behalf they are used. An employee or
contractor using the Kit for an organization must assess that organization's
eligibility, not just the employee's or contractor's personal income. A person's
unrelated employer is not counted for genuinely independent personal use.

"Business Use" means use in a business, professional practice, or an
organization's operations, including internal model production, commissioned
work, sales of models or content, and incorporation into a product or service.
It includes development and testing for those activities, whether or not a
particular project has earned revenue yet.

"Revenue" means gross business revenue, before expenses and excluding consumption
or sales taxes collected on behalf of tax authorities, across Your business as
a whole, not just the Kit-based project. Use Your most recently completed fiscal
year: the regular annual accounting period used for Your business, not a period
chosen solely for this License. For an independent individual, use the most
recently completed calendar year unless the business uses another regular
fiscal year. For a business without a defined fiscal year, use the immediately
preceding twelve months. If no fiscal year has yet ended, use actual revenue
since the business began, limited to the immediately preceding twelve months.
Do not annualize revenue for a business operating for less than twelve months
or for a short initial fiscal year. An independent individual's unrelated
employment salary and personal transfers are not business revenue.

"Funding" means the cumulative external equity investment and business-purpose
loan proceeds actually received since Your business began, including convertible
financing. It is not limited to the preceding twelve months. Exclude revenue,
an individual founder's unborrowed personal funds contributed to a business
independently owned and controlled by that founder,
personal borrowing unrelated to the business, and non-repayable grants or gifts.
Do not count a refinancing of the same outstanding principal twice; count any
additional proceeds. Repayment or spending of funds does not reduce this
cumulative amount.

For an organization under common control with other entities, assess Revenue
and Funding across that controlled group, excluding transfers within the group
to avoid double counting. Control means majority ownership or the power to
direct management. Splitting a business into projects or controlled entities
does not create separate free allowances.

If entities in a controlled group have different fiscal year-end dates, use
each entity's most recently completed fiscal year and reassess group Revenue
whenever any such fiscal year ends. Apply the rules above to any group entity
without a defined or completed fiscal year.

The financial threshold is JPY 100,000,000. Revenue and Funding are tested
separately, not added together: reaching either threshold is sufficient.
For amounts in other currencies, use a consistently applied, publicly available
exchange-rate source and the rate on the date each amount was recognized or
received. Keep sufficient records to explain Your eligibility if reasonably
requested; this License does not authorize access to Your accounting systems.

2. Free permission

Subject to this License, You may download, install, run, privately copy, inspect,
and modify the Covered Materials without a license fee if:

(a) Your use is genuinely personal and outside Business Use; or
(b) both Your Revenue and Your Funding are below the financial threshold.

This permission includes eligible Business Use, internal production, use with
AI agents and Blender, and operation of a hosted service on infrastructure
under Your control. Making Kit code available to customers, including delivering
the application to their browsers, is redistribution and requires Section 4
permission even if Your business qualifies for free use.

You may provide the necessary private copies to personnel and infrastructure
or AI service providers acting solely to carry out Your permitted use, subject
to confidentiality and no independent reuse of the Covered Materials. This is
not permission to publish the Kit or grant customers copies or independent
rights. You remain responsible for keeping this use within Your permission.

Free use requires no registration or license payment. It remains subject to
the redistribution restrictions. There is no limit here on the number or price
of models You may create, but business model sales count toward Revenue.

3. Business Use requiring a separate commercial agreement

If Your Revenue OR Your Funding is JPY 100,000,000 or more, You must obtain a
separate written commercial agreement from the Licensor before Business Use.
This applies to both internal production and product or service integration,
including Business Use by an individual. Downloading an update, sending an
inquiry, or receiving an invoice alone does not authorize such use.

Assess Your eligibility before starting Business Use. Reassess Revenue at the
end of each fiscal year; the new assessment applies from the start of the next
fiscal year, without waiting for tax filing or formal approval of accounts.
Until then, use the same most recently completed fiscal year: revenue earned
during the current fiscal year alone does not change that assessment. If You
have no defined fiscal year or no completed fiscal year, monitor actual Revenue
using the periods defined in Section 1; reaching the threshold in that period
requires an agreement before further Business Use.

Funding is cumulative and does not use a fiscal-year or twelve-month period.
Reassess Funding when additional qualifying funds are received; reaching its
threshold requires an agreement before further Business Use, even during a
fiscal year in which Your Revenue remains below the threshold.

If You reach a threshold while using the Kit under Section 2, obtain that
agreement before continuing Business Use. Earlier use that complied with this
License is not retroactively charged. No automatic grace period, commercial
trial, or evaluation-use exception is granted; any such permission must be
given in writing. Reading the public source, GitHub activities under Section 4,
and retaining an inactive archival copy do not themselves require a paid
commercial agreement.

Fees, duration, authorized users, integration scope, and any redistribution
rights are negotiated in that agreement. This License sets no fixed price,
per-user charge, automatic renewal, or obligation to offer an agreement.
Unless expressly agreed otherwise, a commercial arrangement covers only the
specified usage rights and access to publicly released updates during its term.
It includes no individual support, setup assistance, commissioned production,
custom development, guaranteed results, or promise of future updates.

On expiry of a commercial agreement, Business Use must stop unless You have
renewed, have other written permission, or then qualify under Section 2.
Authorized Outputs remain subject to Section 6, not a continuing Kit fee.

4. GitHub forks, contributions, and redistribution

You may view and fork the public repository within GitHub, retain and modify
such forks there, and submit issues, patches, and pull requests. This permission
applies regardless of the financial threshold. It does not permit otherwise
restricted Business Use. Nothing here narrows rights granted by the applicable
GitHub Terms of Service for GitHub's operation of public repositories.

Retain this License and existing copyright, attribution, and third-party
notices with the Covered Materials. Clearly identify material changes and
identify a modified fork as unofficial. Include this License when permitted
copies of individual Skills or other Covered Materials are supplied separately.

Except for the GitHub repository activities above and private operational
copies under Section 2, redistribution requires prior written permission from
the Licensor. This includes free or paid copies, reposting on other sites,
mirrors outside GitHub, re-uploaded ZIPs, package registries, installers, bundled
applications, and independently distributed modified releases. The fork
exception is not permission to publish separate release packages, downloads,
or a hosted app from a fork, including through GitHub Releases or GitHub Pages.

A commercial license fee does not by itself authorize redistribution. Any
redistribution permission must identify its scope. Unless that permission
expressly provides otherwise, every permitted redistribution of Covered
Materials, modified or not, must include this License and remain subject to its
conditions. Recipients need their own permission for use outside this License.

