* Orbitron font: public/fonts/Orbitron-OFL.txt (SIL Open Font License 1.1).

Preserve those notices. Other identified third-party licenses also prevail
for their respective components.

Project-supplied bundled assets include example characters and models,
reference artwork, screenshots, thumbnails, GIFs, videos, promotional graphics,
logos, and the weighted donor body. They are provided for the Kit's workflow
and documentation only. You must not extract those assets for standalone use
outside the Kit, take or upload them to external services for independent use,
or redistribute them separately. This prohibition applies to commercial and
non-commercial use; a commercial software agreement does not grant those rights.

You may view the documentation and preserve it together with its embedded media
in a GitHub fork permitted by Section 4. A weighted donor body supplied by the
rights holder for this Kit may be loaded and modified locally only for body
fitting and weight transfer, with local intermediate copies as needed. The
donor, its meshes, rig, and intermediate fitted copies must not be taken out
for independent use or distributed separately. This grants no rights in
third-party donor material.

These restrictions do not apply to Your own authorized Outputs under Section 6
or override separately licensed third-party components. Tripo sponsor logos
remain Tripo-owned; preserve their original colors and proportions when showing
them for sponsor attribution. No right to reuse those logos independently is
granted.

No trademark or endorsement rights are granted. ELYTH, Tripo, OpenAI, Blender,
and other names remain subject to their respective owners' rights. Sponsorship
does not imply ownership, support obligations, or endorsement of modified forks.
External services and tools require their own accounts, terms, and fees.

9. Breach and termination

Permission under this License ends if You materially breach its conditions.
You must stop the activities for which You no longer have permission and remove
unauthorized distributions under Your control. If You cure the breach within
30 days after receiving written notice of it, permission is reinstated unless
You previously received a notice of the same type of breach. Otherwise,
reinstatement requires written permission. Cure does not authorize unlicensed
use during the breach or waive claims arising from it. A separate commercial
agreement may specify its own termination and cure rules.

The provisions about retained notices, ownership, authorized Outputs,
third-party rights, disclaimers, and liability continue as applicable after
termination. Non-waivable rights under applicable law are unaffected.

